// CutScene 
// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// 4 Caption :
"P3987753757" "<x=0.3 y=0.3 d=4 t=4><scale 2.75><color White><bgcolor black>Reese, the 'Top Dog' of the Powers Division, failed in his attempt to kill you..."
// 4 Caption :
"P3764520679" "<x=0.7 y=0.3 d=4 t=4><scale 2.75><color White><bgcolor Black>The bombs he intended to use to blow you up - along with this warehouse - still remain usable..."
// 4 Caption :
"P2336366131" "<x=0.5 y=0.3 d=4 t=4><scale 2.75><color White><bgcolor Black>But will you seek vengeance on Reese...or use this to gain more power within the Powers Division?"
// LeftText :
"P3606898077" "<scale 2.5><span align=center><color Paragon>Blow Up Reese</color></scale><br>Set the bombs in the warehouse to explode, killing Reese and his men</span><br><br><color Paragon>Gain power within Resistance</color><br>Blowing up Reese and his boys won't earn you any points within the Loyalists. It certainly would give you a good amount of power and sway within the Resistance if they knew you single-handedly took down seven members of the Powers Division. Is it worth more to hold power within the Resistance, or within the Loyalists?<br><br><scale .8><color slategray><i>(As the story of Praetoria unfolds your character will have opportunities to change their mind and switch sides.)</i></scale>"
// RightText :
"P3709567816" "<scale 2.5><span align=center><color orange>Report Your Victory</color></scale><br>Call in Praetor White to witness what happened</span><br><br><color orange>Gain power within the Loyalists</color><br>Reese's pride got the better of him. He thought this puny force was enough to take you down, but he was wrong. Someone needs to personally show Praetor White that, maybe, Reese isn't all that. You could easily contact Praetor White to get him down here and see just what happens when someone tries to double cross you. After this stunt, you'll easily gain Reese's position - and more - within the Loyalists.<br><br><i><scale .8><color slategray>(As the story of Praetoria unfolds your character will have opportunities to change their mind and switch sides.)</scale></i>"

